{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-leader-variant.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 43 fixed the binding shape and submitted the promoted-leader variant as a formal check.\\n\\nWhat was wrong last turn. The rejected attempts failed because the monitors' own grounding objects still carried the previous plan's binding id (the divergence plan's BB2-prepare-resolution) while the plan-level lists pointed elsewhere — so the check both used a non-selected binding and left a grounding reference to an unavailable one. The successful shape, as in the earlier obligations, is to point every binding reference at the same newly supplied binding: the claim's grounding, the plan's binding_ids, each monitor's binding_ids, each monitor's grounding.binding_ids and the harness legality.\\n\\nWhat was submitted. A new obligation C6-recovery-ignores-committed-reply-when-promoted (consensus safety, priority 3): when the replica the deployment promoted to leader (IsLeader true, with a ballot history above its ballot base) recovers an instance and a slow-quorum reply reports it COMMITTED, the recovering replica must adopt that committed vector rather than restarting phase 1 with a different command. Its scope is the promoted variant only, with the non-promoted case left to C1, and it is grounded on a new binding (BB7-leader-variant) that documents startRecoveryForInstance's raised ballot and the self VBallot it publishes. The plan carries the three properties already reviewed for the non-promoted case (adoption at the resolution, the recoverer-versus-committed-peer comparison, agreement across replicas after the Commit broadcast), with the promoted-variant semantic change and a controls note that the seed event prints is_leader, max_recv_ballot, the seed ballot and the self VBallot. The harness is the reviewed driven variant with IsLeader true and maxRecvBallot set above the ballot base.\\n\\nWhy it matters. The shipped aws.conf designates a leader and the master promotes through Replica.BeTheLeader, so this variant is the deployed case rather than an artificial one. The local construction run showed the same masking (new ballot 6 reported as the self VBallot, adopted_committed false, accept round completing, vectors_match false, all_committed_match false, applied state diverging), so the formal outcome is expected to be violated and awaits the trusted runner plus a fresh correspondence review. Claim C1 and the other settled claims are untouched, and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
